meta {
  name: Start Response Rejection
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/start?ipas={{brotliIpaCode}}&status=Initial
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  ipas: {{brotliIpaCode}}
  status: Initial
}

tests {
  test("The negative fixture was selected and queued", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(202);
    expect(res.getBody()).to.be.an("array");
    expect(res.getBody()).to.include(bru.getEnvVar("brotliIpaCode"));
  });
}

docs {
  Local-only response validation test using benign compressed data.
  Build, seed, and restart the updated local launcher first.
  The local SelfcareMock sends a non-identity encoded response for fiscal code
  00000000001, even though the worker requests Accept-Encoding: identity.

  This 202 confirms only submission. Inspect the selected membership in
  importadesioni-local / memberships in Cosmos: expect Failed and a note
  containing Unsupported Content-Encoding. Processed would fail this test.

  Do not also submit the same negative fixture through the command-line checker.
  Changing Accept-Encoding on the incoming Bruno request is not equivalent:
  response validation applies to the downstream SelfCare response path.
}